  "details": "currently the quest shaders built for the platform are severely lacking and even outdated. standard lite definitely hates light (i wanted white skin not the surface of the sun!) and transparent particle shaders that are OFFICIALLY SUPPORTED. (and actually give you full transparency.) one shader example would be one that is very easy to add seeing as you have all 3 of the components in existing shaders. base+emissions+matcap\nmatcap lit emissive could definitely be useful for certain avatars. or how about working on remaking standard lite to have more accurate lighting using baked lightmaps. ect ect...",
